                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A perfect conclusion for the Sky trilogy. It sorta serves as a epilogue for the people that enjoy the cast while adding more depth into Kevin's character. It also plants the seeds for future Trails games through dialogue and Star and Moon Doors (Sun Doors are more so like minigames) that contain short stories that are essential to the world-building and future arcs. The main story is a bit on the shorter side and the game is structured like a linear dungeon crawler with a large pool of characters that unlock the more you progress. The combat is more polished with crazy difficulty curves in some boss fights. It is the toughest of all in the Sky games. Overall it's such a great game and had a blast from it besides chapter 6's pacing being sluggish.\n Whoever came up that this is the skippable Trails game, they're crazy.",
